<%# The account entries at the foot of the side navigation (decision: directly in the bar, no menu to open:
    only two actions).
    On a phone, the gear of the settings page, like the other icons of the floating bar (log out is there too,
    in Account; decision: the gear rather than the avatar).
    From 768 px: "Settings", which opens the settings window (settings_link_data), or the settings page when already
    on it; "Log out"; then the avatar and the username, which only show who is signed in %>
<div class="md:hidden">
  <%= side_nav_link_to t(".settings"), settings_path, icon: "settings", current: settings_page? %>
</div>

<%# Under "My tables", at the foot of the bar (shared/_side_nav). No margin of its own: every entry of the foot is
    6 px from the next one, the gap of the bar (a margin here doubled it, decision) %>
<div class="hidden md:flex md:flex-col md:gap-1.5">
  <%= side_nav_link_to t(".settings"), settings_display_path, icon: "settings", current: settings_page?,
                                                              data: settings_link_data %>
  <%# Asked first (shared/_confirm_dialog): a stray click in the bar no longer signs out %>
  <%= side_nav_button_to t(".log_out"), destroy_user_session_path, icon: "log_out", method: :delete,
                                                                    confirm: t(".log_out_confirmation") %>

  <%= render "shared/account_identity" %>
</div>
